      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "First, make sure you have the status of being able to upload avatars.  It will tell you at the top of the VRC SDK Upload Control Panel before you push \"Build and Publish\"\n\nI've seen this a few times for other people.  I've seen where someone is trying to upload, it completes and doesn't give an error message.  Make sure you have a clean, new copy of the SDK.\n\nIf you're using a character package and it already contains the SDK, open it and export the character / materials / shaders / etc, but not the VRCSDK files.\n\nDownload a brand new copy of the VRCSDK to your machine.\n\nOpen a new project, import the character.  Then import the new SDK you downloaded.\n\nI've seen this clean this issue, hope it helps for you.  Sorry if it doesn't fix your problem.\n\nFlay",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
